---
number: 416
title: Who, Who Are These?
author: Tullius C. O’Kane
composer: T. C. O’Kane
sp_category: "25"
topic: Salvation
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
Who, who are these raised up to endless joy,
Whose faith is pure as gold without alloy,
Which no foe could e’er destroy,
Washed in the blood of the Lamb.

[chorus]
Sweeping thro’ the gates to the New Jerusalem,
Washed in the blood of the Lamb,
(in the blood of the Lamb).
Sweeping thro’ the gates to the New Jerusalem,
Washed in the blood of the Lamb.

[verse 2]
These, these are they who in their youthful days
Found Jesus early, and in wisdom’s ways
Proved the fulness of His grace.
Washed in the blood of the Lamb.

[chorus]
Sweeping thro’ the gates to the New Jerusalem,
Washed in the blood of the Lamb,
(in the blood of the Lamb).
Sweeping thro’ the gates to the New Jerusalem,
Washed in the blood of the Lamb.

[verse 3]
These, these are they who in affliction’s woes,
Ever have found in Jesus calm repose,
Peace which from a pure heart flows.
Washed in the blood of the Lamb.

[chorus]
Sweeping thro’ the gates to the New Jerusalem,
Washed in the blood of the Lamb,
(in the blood of the Lamb).
Sweeping thro’ the gates to the New Jerusalem,
Washed in the blood of the Lamb.

[verse 4]
Safe, safe upon the evershining shore,
Sin, pain, and death, and sorrow all are o’er;
Happy now and evermore,
Washed in the blood of the Lamb.

[chorus]
Sweeping thro’ the gates to the New Jerusalem,
Washed in the blood of the Lamb,
(in the blood of the Lamb).
Sweeping thro’ the gates to the New Jerusalem,
Washed in the blood of the Lamb.
